lowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T10:53:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-15T10:53:04Z","body":"I have no idea why I didn’t write this earlier, but basically, if this doesn’t work for you on X11, then we can probably assume that a large portion of these errors happens specifically on the Awesome window manager or something similar, since that’s what I’m using.  \n  \nWhat I mean is this: either the issue is related to how X11 behaves after many panels became floating/free around version 4.1, which introduced a lot of bugs like this, or this is simply how tiling/floating window managers behave, since they really are quite “free” in that regard.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4459146747/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4512830480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118553#issuecomment-4512830480","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118553","id":4512830480,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDPxUEA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"http